    {
      "id": "EV3kVScKxeBwxp-Duq6AN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 37.67161184287113,
      "y": 6317.905424718039,
      "width": 718.3394165039062,
      "height": 3100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 305723924,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 404555308,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1770079392846,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ LIVE DEPLOYMENT – IMPORTANT POINTS (NO BASH)\n🧠 1. Architecture clear rakho\n\nFrontend, Backend aur Database alag-alag cheezein hain\n\nFrontend kabhi directly database se connect nahi karta\n\nData hamesha: Frontend → Backend → Database\n\n📂 2. Folder structure sahi hona chahiye\n\nFrontend aur Backend alag folders me hone chahiye\n\nBackend ko frontend ke andar mat rakho\n\n🐳 3. Docker ka basic rule\n\nDockerfile ka matlab app chal rahi hai — galat\n\nApp tab chalti hai jab container run hota hai\n\nImage aur container alag concepts hain\n\n🔄 4. Code update ka sahi flow\n\nCode change ke baad:\n\nImage rebuild karni padti hai\n\nContainer restart / recreate karna padta hai\n\nSirf git pull kaafi nahi hota\n\n🌐 5. Ports ka dhyaan rakho\n\nFrontend aur Backend same port pe kabhi nahi chalte\n\nHar service ka alag port hota hai\n\nBrowser se backend open hona zaroori hai\n\n🔐 6. Environment variables (bahut important)\n\nSecrets (DB URL, passwords) code me hardcode nahi\n\nBackend me env se:\n\nPORT\n\nMongoDB URI\n\nFrontend me env se:\n\nBackend API URL\n\n🗄 7. MongoDB Atlas ke rules\n\nAtlas ka username/password EC2 ya system se alag hota hai\n\nPassword kabhi screen pe show nahi hota\n\nNetwork Access me IP allow karna zaroori hai\n\nDatabase tabhi kaam karega jab backend live ho\n\n🧱 8. Backend start hone ki conditions\n\nBackend ki main file ka naam/path exact match kare\n\nLinux case-sensitive hota hai\n\nBackend localhost pe bind nahi hona chahiye\n\n🔁 9. CORS ka dhyaan rakho\n\nFrontend aur backend alag ports pe ho to CORS allow hona chahiye\n\nJSON body parsing enabled hona chahiye\n\n🌍 10. Cloud firewall (EC2 Security Group)\n\nPorts manually allow karne padte hain\n\nAgar port allow nahi hai to app open nahi hogi\n\nYeh OS firewall se alag hota hai\n\n🧪 11. Live hone ka real test\n\nFrontend URL browser me open ho\n\nBackend URL pe response aaye\n\nAPI hit karne pe database me data dikhe\n\n❌ 12. Common galtiyan (avoid karo)\n\nFrontend me localhost use karna\n\nEnv change ke baad rebuild na karna\n\nBackend image build kiye bina run karna\n\nGalat file names / paths\n\nMongoDB password galat ya special characters ke saath encode na karna\n\n🧠 13. Debugging mindset\n\nPehle check karo app chal rahi hai ya nahi\n\nPhir ports open hain ya nahi\n\nPhir logs dekho\n\nHar problem ek hi jagah se nahi hoti\n\n🏆 14. Interview-level understanding\n\nFrontend and backend independently deployable hone chahiye\n\nDatabase access sirf backend ke paas hota hai\n\nDeployment zyada configuration ka game hai, sirf coding ka nahi",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ LIVE DEPLOYMENT – IMPORTANT POINTS (NO BASH)\n🧠 1. Architecture clear rakho\n\nFrontend, Backend aur Database alag-alag cheezein hain\n\nFrontend kabhi directly database se connect nahi karta\n\nData hamesha: Frontend → Backend → Database\n\n📂 2. Folder structure sahi hona chahiye\n\nFrontend aur Backend alag folders me hone chahiye\n\nBackend ko frontend ke andar mat rakho\n\n🐳 3. Docker ka basic rule\n\nDockerfile ka matlab app chal rahi hai — galat\n\nApp tab chalti hai jab container run hota hai\n\nImage aur container alag concepts hain\n\n🔄 4. Code update ka sahi flow\n\nCode change ke baad:\n\nImage rebuild karni padti hai\n\nContainer restart / recreate karna padta hai\n\nSirf git pull kaafi nahi hota\n\n🌐 5. Ports ka dhyaan rakho\n\nFrontend aur Backend same port pe kabhi nahi chalte\n\nHar service ka alag port hota hai\n\nBrowser se backend open hona zaroori hai\n\n🔐 6. Environment variables (bahut important)\n\nSecrets (DB URL, passwords) code me hardcode nahi\n\nBackend me env se:\n\nPORT\n\nMongoDB URI\n\nFrontend me env se:\n\nBackend API URL\n\n🗄 7. MongoDB Atlas ke rules\n\nAtlas ka username/password EC2 ya system se alag hota hai\n\nPassword kabhi screen pe show nahi hota\n\nNetwork Access me IP allow karna zaroori hai\n\nDatabase tabhi kaam karega jab backend live ho\n\n🧱 8. Backend start hone ki conditions\n\nBackend ki main file ka naam/path exact match kare\n\nLinux case-sensitive hota hai\n\nBackend localhost pe bind nahi hona chahiye\n\n🔁 9. CORS ka dhyaan rakho\n\nFrontend aur backend alag ports pe ho to CORS allow hona chahiye\n\nJSON body parsing enabled hona chahiye\n\n🌍 10. Cloud firewall (EC2 Security Group)\n\nPorts manually allow karne padte hain\n\nAgar port allow nahi hai to app open nahi hogi\n\nYeh OS firewall se alag hota hai\n\n🧪 11. Live hone ka real test\n\nFrontend URL browser me open ho\n\nBackend URL pe response aaye\n\nAPI hit karne pe database me data dikhe\n\n❌ 12. Common galtiyan (avoid karo)\n\nFrontend me localhost use karna\n\nEnv change ke baad rebuild na karna\n\nBackend image build kiye bina run karna\n\nGalat file names / paths\n\nMongoDB password galat ya special characters ke saath encode na karna\n\n🧠 13. Debugging mindset\n\nPehle check karo app chal rahi hai ya nahi\n\nPhir ports open hain ya nahi\n\nPhir logs dekho\n\nHar problem ek hi jagah se nahi hoti\n\n🏆 14. Interview-level understanding\n\nFrontend and backend independently deployable hone chahiye\n\nDatabase access sirf backend ke paas hota hai\n\nDeployment zyada configuration ka game hai, sirf coding ka nahi",
